# November 19, 2026: Licking County, Ohio (Newark, Heath, Granville, Hebron, Buckeye Lake, Outville, the Blackhand Gorge
# and Flint Ridge), with the Deep Cut of the Ohio and Erie Canal just over the line at Millersport, Fairfield County.
# Region drawn at random by tools/choose.py (oh); the county by a random draw.
# Sources read in this session: Wikipedia articles (tools/wiki_raw.py), HMdb marker pages (full inscriptions and
# positions, tools/page.py), the Ohio DNR pages for the Blackhand Gorge preserve and Buckeye Lake State Park, the
# Hopewell Ceremonial Earthworks site, WYSU and WYSO news reports on the Octagon opening, the Licking County Records and
# Archives blog, the National Trust's 2026 story on the Sullivan bank, the Bryn Du Commission's site and the Robbins
# Hunter Museum's visit page. The Ohio History Connection's own pages (ohiohistory.org) answered HTTP 403 with no
# archived copy, so the hours of the Great Circle and Flint Ridge were not checked.
